	<ehr:termdefinition.dp.language>en</ehr:termdefinition.dp.language>
	<ehr:termdefinition.dp.text>Intersex or indeterminate</ehr:termdefinition.dp.text>
	<ehr:termdefinition.dp.description>is normally used for babies for whom sex has not been determined for whatever reason, should not generally be used on data collection forms completed by the respondent and should only be used if the person or respondent volunteers that the person is intersex or where it otherwise becomes clear during the collection process that the individual is neither male nor female</ehr:termdefinition.dp.description>
</rdf:Description>

