<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://bki.skane.se/ikm/id/ikmopenehr:modeldescription/splash-adl2-tpl/openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.adverse.v1.0.0/description/en">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://bki.skane.se/ikm/ont/ikmopenehr:modeldescription"/>
	<rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Adverse reaction</rdfs:label>
	<ikm:thing.dp.kgdisplay>Adverse reaction</ikm:thing.dp.kgdisplay>
	<ikm:thing.dp.kguri rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://bki.skane.se/ikm/id/ikmopenehr:modeldescription/splash-adl2-tpl/openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.adverse.v1.0.0/description/en</ikm:thing.dp.kguri>
	<ehr:openehrobject.op.module rdf:resource="http://bki.skane.se/ikm/id/kg__module/openehr-draft-example"/>
	<ehr:modelelement.op.owner rdf:resource="http://bki.skane.se/ikm/id/ikmopenehr:archetype/splash-adl2-tpl/openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.adverse.v1.0.0"/>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.language>en</ehr:modeldescription.dp.language>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.name>Adverse reaction</ehr:modeldescription.dp.name>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.description>Recording the presence of a harmful or undesirable response to an agent or substance including food, as determined by the clinician - excluding poisoning and abnormal use</ehr:modeldescription.dp.description>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.purpose>For recording all adverse reaction(s) to a particular 'Agent', whether an individual agent or substance, or a class.  
Recordings may be added for subsequent exposures to the same Agent and the type of reaction on each occasion, building up a persisting record over time.</ehr:modeldescription.dp.purpose>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.use>Use to record exposure to agents and the adverse reaction that occurs. 
If recording an adverse event to a class or grouping of 'Agent', then exposure to different specific components of the class can be recorded as well.  For example, recording against the class of Penicillin it is possible to record the reaction (or absence) to specific types or brands of Penicillin. </ehr:modeldescription.dp.use>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.misuse>Not to be used for recording the exclusion of a history of a reaction to a substance. Use openEHR-EVALUATION.excluded-adverse for this purpose.</ehr:modeldescription.dp.misuse>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>reaction</ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>allergic</ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>allergy</ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>intolerance</ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>
	<ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>adverse</ehr:modeldescription.dp.keywords>
</rdf:Description>

